  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/medicine_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B024",
        "laureates": [
          "Kazutoshi Mori",
          "Peter Walter"
        ],
        "citation": "for discoveries of the unfolded protein response and signaling from the endoplasmic reticulum"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B022",
    "B045"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B024 recognizes a discrete, fundamental and long-established physiological mechanism by which cells sense and adapt to endoplasmic-reticulum stress. The supplied discussion supports its mechanistic maturity, broad influence on proteostasis and cell state, and a compact proposed attribution to Mori and Walter. Unlike configurations framed around later therapeutic development, its citation can remain confined to the foundational signaling discovery rather than claiming all downstream disease applications.",
    "case_against": "B024 has less direct demonstrated clinical consequence in the supplied evidence than B022, B045, or B013. Moreover, although Mori and Walter are an appealing two-person allocation, the record supplied here does not resolve the full priority history or establish that no further indispensable contributor would emerge from detailed historical review.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "linnarsson-sten",
        "point": "Linnarsson continues to favor B022 because it links GLP-1 physiology to a broad, mature transformation in diabetes and obesity treatment, while recognizing difficult boundaries among hormone biology, physiology, and pharmaceutical development.",
        "response": "I agree that B022 has extraordinary medical consequences and is a serious alternative. The remaining attribution issue is material: the proposed achievement traverses hormone identification, physiological interpretation, translational work, peptide engineering, and a wider development pathway. B024 more readily identifies a delimited discovery and a compact pair, so I continue to give mechanistic clarity and attributional coherence greater weight than the more direct therapeutic reach of B022."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "perlmann-thomas",
        "point": "Perlmann favors B045 for its mature preventive effect against HPV-related cancers, while emphasizing the need to separate vaccine-enabling VLP work from papillomavirus biology, product development, and implementation.",
        "response": "The preventive significance of B045 is exceptional, and the proposed VLP-centered citation is appropriately narrower than a general cancer-prevention claim. Still, the discussion leaves unresolved whether Lowy, Frazer, and Schiller precisely capture the vaccine-enabling discovery once foundational biology and subsequent development are separated. B024's direct mechanistic definition and two-person proposed credit remain stronger on the present evidence."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "wahren-herlenius-marie",
        "point": "Wahren-Herlenius prioritizes B013 because TNF blockade connects a defined pathogenic mechanism to durable disease-modifying treatment, with Feldmann and Maini as a focused proposed pair.",
        "response": "B013 is a compelling mechanism-to-treatment achievement with mature clinical validation and an admirably focused attribution. I nevertheless retain B024 because the unfolded protein response is a more fundamental and broadly explanatory cellular principle; its medical importance need not be inflated into direct therapeutic claims to be awardable. The need to distinguish Feldmann and Maini's central work from wider anti-TNF development also remains unresolved."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether detailed historical review would confirm that Mori and Walter alone capture all indispensable foundational contributions to unfolded-protein-response signaling.",
      "Whether the direct, mature medical outcomes of B022, B045, or B013 should outweigh B024's more fundamental but less clinically direct achievement.",
      "Whether B022 and B045 can each be delimited and attributed without incorporating later pharmaceutical development, product development, or implementation."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent from the supplied profile. My documented co-authorship with Sten Linnarsson and Jonas Frisén, and the shared KI single-cell genomics setting, identify no connection to any proposed candidate."
  }
}
